OSaaS-01

Self Serve Capability
As an Application Team member,
I want to be able to request the upgrade of my EC2 instances using ServiceNow,
So that upgrades don't have to be done manually, saving British Airways significant time and money as well as ensuring that mandatory Cyber security and patching standards are adhered to through ECP provided tooling.

Scenario: Accessing the request form

Given that I am an authenticated and authorised user

When I access the OS Upgrade ServiceNow form

Then I am presented with a drop-down list of AWS accounts that are valid for upgrades.

Scenario: Instance selection and metadata display

Given that I am on the OS Upgrade ServiceNow form

When I select a valid AWS account

Then I am presented with a list of EC2 Instances including their OS, Instance Type, IP Address, Tags, Security Groups, and Volumes.

Scenario: Target Operating System selection

Given that I have selected one or more EC2 Instances

When I select a target operating system

Then the options are restricted to the correct OS family based on the available Cyber-authorised Golden Images provided by ECP.

Scenario: Middleware selection

Given that I have selected a valid target operating system

When I am prompted for software requirements

Then I am presented with a list of appropriate middleware compatible with that OS.

Scenario: Production Workload Acknowledgement

Given that I have selected an EC2 instance tagged as 'Production'

When I attempt to proceed with the request

Then the system displays a mandatory warning box regarding Production risk.

Scenario: Production Responsibility Acceptance

Given that the Production warning box is displayed

When I attempt to submit the form

Then the system requires a mandatory "I accept responsibility for this Production upgrade" tick-box to be checked.

Scenario: Data-Containing Server Acknowledgement

Given that I am submitting an upgrade request

When I proceed to the final submission step

Then the system displays a mandatory warning box regarding local persistent data.

Scenario: Data Loss Responsibility Acceptance

Given that the data-containing server warning is displayed

When I attempt to submit the form

Then the system requires a mandatory "I confirm this server stores no local persistent data and I accept responsibility for any data loss" tick-box to be checked.

Scenario: Form submitted

Given that I have successfully submitted the form

When it is a valid and complete instruction set

Then a ServiceNow upgrade task is created and triggered.




OSaaS-02

Automated Infrastructure Provisioning
As an Application Team member,
I want the system to automatically provision a new instance that meets the mandatory Cyber security and patching standards implemented via ECP tooling,
So that my application is moved away from insecure, legacy operating systems.

Scenario: Provisioning with Latest Golden Image

Given that a valid upgrade task has been triggered

When the system starts the build

Then a new EC2 instance is created using the latest ECP-provided Golden Image authorised by Cyber for the selected OS.

Scenario: Enforcement of Cyber Patching Standards

Given that a new EC2 instance is provisioned

When the instance is initialised

Then the system applies the Cyber-authorised patching configuration using ECP platform tooling.

Scenario: Instance Type Matching

Given that the new EC2 instance is being provisioned

When the system selects the hardware size

Then the Instance Type of the new server matches the Instance Type of the source server.

Scenario: Notification of new Golden Image

Given that a new version of the golden image has been produced by the ECP team

When the golden image is approved and published

Then a notification must be sent to relevant teams

And the notification must include the golden image version

And the notification must include the release date.




OSaaS-03

Access and Metadata Replication
As an Application Team member,
I want the new instance to retain the access permissions of the original server,
So that network and identity connectivity is maintained while the underlying OS is upgraded to a secure standard.

Scenario: Tag replication

Given that the new EC2 instance is being provisioned

When the build process is active

Then the system copies all Tags from the source instance to the target instance.

Scenario: Security Group replication

Given that the new EC2 instance is being provisioned

When the system configures network access

Then the system applies the exact Security Groups from the source instance to the target instance.

Scenario: IAM Role replication

Given that the new EC2 instance is being provisioned

When the system configures identity access

Then the system applies the exact IAM Role from the source instance to the target instance.




OSaaS-04

Storage and Configuration Replication
As an Application Team member,
I want my storage volumes and application settings to be replicated to the new secure instance,
So that the service can be validated quickly.

Scenario: EBS Volume replication

Given that the new EC2 instance has been created

When the system identifies the EBS volumes on the source instance

Then the system creates new EBS volumes of the same size and type as the source.

Scenario: EBS Volume attachment

Given that new EBS volumes have been created

When the target instance is ready for storage

Then the system attaches these volumes to the target instance in the correct mount positions.

Scenario: Middleware installation

Given that the new EC2 instance is running

When the build reaches the software phase

Then the system installs the middleware packages selected in the ServiceNow form.

Scenario: Configuration file transfer

Given that the new EC2 instance has been created

And the middleware has been installed

When the system initiates the data sync

Then the system copies the relevant application configuration files to the equivalent locations on the target instance.

Scenario: Service initiation

Given that the configuration files have been copied

When the configuration phase is complete

Then the system attempts to start the application services on the target instance.




OSaaS-05

Server Compliance and Security Enablement
As an Application Team member,
I want servers to be automatically configured, validated, and enrolled into operational and security services,
So that they are consistently compliant, secure, and ready for use without manual intervention or risk exposure.

Scenario: Compliance Visibility

Given that multiple servers have been onboarded

When compliance status is reviewed

Then each server has a visible compliance status

And non-compliant servers clearly identify failed steps.

Scenario: End-to-End Compliance Validation

Given that all onboarding steps have been executed

When the server is assessed for readiness

Then the server is marked as compliant only if all steps have passed

And any failed step results in a non-compliant status

And the failure reason is visible and traceable.

Scenario: Enrolment into Patching Service

Given that the server is successfully registered

When the onboarding process completes

Then the server is enrolled into the patching service

And only validated and registered servers are eligible for enrolment

And any enrolment failures are identified and flagged.

Scenario: Relevant Services Started

Given that the OS and middleware baseline is successfully established

When the onboarding process continues

Then all services relevant to the server role are started

And services not relevant to the server role are not started

And any failure to start a required service is logged and flagged.

Scenario: OS and Middleware Baseline Established

Given that a server has been provisioned

When the onboarding process is initiated

Then the required operating system services are running

And the required middleware components are active

And any missing or failed services are identified and flagged.




OSaaS-06

Handover and Status Reporting
As an Application Team member,
I want to be notified of the build status via ServiceNow,
So that I can manage my manual testing and cutover activities.

Scenario: Build Progress Update

Given that the OSaaS system is performing the build

When an automated step completes

Then the system updates the ServiceNow task status log.

Scenario: Technical detail handover - Instance ID

Given that the build is marked as complete

When the user views the ServiceNow task

Then the system displays the New Instance ID.

Scenario: Technical detail handover - IP Address

Given that the build is marked as complete

When the user views the ServiceNow task

Then the system displays the New IP Address.




OSaaS-07

Controlled Decommissioning
As an Application Team member,
I want to control the lifecycle of the legacy server,
So that I can ensure the old, insecure OS is removed from the network once I have confirmed the new server is functional.

Scenario: Stopping the legacy instance

Given that the user has confirmed the upgrade is successful in ServiceNow

When the system processes the confirmation

Then the system triggers a "Stop" command on the source EC2 instance.

Scenario: Verification of Stop state

Given that the system has issued a Stop command

When the instance reaches the 'Stopped' state

Then the system updates the ServiceNow task status to "Old Instance Stopped."

Scenario: Rejection - Instance Termination

Given that the user finds a fault and rejects the upgrade

When the rejection is processed

Then the system terminates the new EC2 instance.

Scenario: Rejection - Mandatory Feedback

Given that the user rejects the upgrade

When the user clicks "Reject"

Then the system requires a mandatory text reason to be provided before the action completes.
